Keep a shared xs as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared ys as an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 1 into xs.
Place 2 into xs.
Place 3 into xs.
Place 1 into ys.
Place 2 into ys.
Place 3 into ys.
Keep a shared linefirst as 0.
Keep a shared linesecond as 0.
Keep a shared linecount as 0.
Keep a shared best as 0.
Keep a shared lastpoint as 0.
Set best to 1.
Set lastpoint to 2.
To check point at spot (a whole number).
The anchor is linefirst.
The other is linesecond.
The dx is item other of xs minus item anchor of xs.
The dy is item other of ys minus item anchor of ys.
The otherx is item spot of xs minus item anchor of xs.
The othery is item spot of ys minus item anchor of ys.
If dx times othery is dy times otherx, add 1 to linecount.

To scan from spot (a whole number).
If spot is more than lastpoint, return.
If spot is not linefirst and spot is not linesecond, check point at spot.
Scan from spot plus 1.

To score from first (a whole number) with second (a whole number).
Set linefirst to first.
Set linesecond to second.
Set linecount to 2.
Scan from 0.
If linecount is more than best, set best to linecount.

For every first from 0 to lastpoint.
For every second from first plus 1 to lastpoint.
Score from first with second.

Show best.
